@talks sato
// TW1, the Talk a while pack: Dr. Imra Sato's own talks (she/her). Fast, clever bursts; starts in the middle; drifts
// mid-thought; explains the tea at length; "No." is a sentence; forgets names, remembers sample numbers. Never that
// the survey she's proudest of was luck (until close); never admits the third comet matters.

== the-tea
topic: food
them: No, the other tea. The good one. Smoked leaf, dried kelp, a pinch of pepper.
them: Nobody else drinks it. I offer it to everyone. It's a test. Mostly of them.   #funny
ask: Will you try it? Honestly. I'll know if you're being polite.
listen: Why kelp, of all things?
  them: Salt, body, and it reminds me of a shore I've never been to. Interesting, no?
share: Go on. One sip.
  them: Good. Brave. Your face is doing something very honest. Write that down. No, I will.   #funny
cheer: Only if I can add a biscuit.
  them: No. Well. Yes, fine. Mori does that too. Mori's wrong. Have a biscuit.   #funny

== comets
topic: work
when: tier>=acquaintance
them: Three comets named. Two of them count. The third one doesn't count.
them: Why not? Because it was small. And late. And. Never mind. It doesn't count.   #funny
ask: What would you name a comet, if you found one?
listen: Why doesn't the third count?
  them: It. Hm. It just doesn't. Next question. Better question.   #funny
share: After someone at home.
  them: Good. That's what most people do. That's what I. Never mind. Good choice.
cheer: Gerald. Obviously.
  them: Ha! The cactus lobby would be thrilled. I'd allow it. Probably.   #funny

== labels
topic: crew
when: tier>=colleague
them: Someone labelled a sample in my store in their own handwriting. Not mine.
them: I've re-labelled it. And the twelve beside it. My store, my handwriting.   #funny
ask: Is there something you're particular about? Very particular?
listen: Does Mori mind?
  them: Mori runs the labs while I run everyone. It works. Don't tell Mori I said "runs".   #funny
share: My toolbelt. Everything in its place.
  them: Good. Order is how you notice the odd thing. The odd thing is the science.
cheer: My place in the dinner queue.
  them: Sensible. Queues are data. I've a chart somewhere. I'll find it. I won't.   #funny

== frontier
topic: plans
when: tier>=friend
them: I turned down a university post to come out here. Everyone said I was mad.
them: Some days I still think they were right. Then I look out of the observatory.   #warm
ask: What made you choose this, out of everything?
listen: Do you ever regret it?
  them: No. Not yet. I say "yet" about most things. It keeps me honest.
share: I wanted to see what's out there.
  them: Good. Same. Now you're in it. Keep looking. Don't stop looking.   #warm
cheer: The tea, clearly. Yours, specifically.
  them: Liar. Kind liar. I'll make you a cup anyway.   #funny
